WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.260
A wedding morning in a gurdwara.

2
00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:06.230
The bride and groom each
hold one end of a long scarf.

3
00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:09.080
A verse is sung as they
walk round the scripture.

4
00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:10.110
Then again.

5
00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:11.970
Four times in all.

6
00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:15.070
When a Sikh dies, there
is no grave to visit.

7
00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:16.390
No headstone.

8
00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:18.820
So why walk round the scripture to marry,

9
00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:20.850
and why no gravestones?

10
00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:25.700
In this mission, you'll hear the Lavan,
four wedding verses by Guru Ram Das.

11
00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:28.440
Then you'll explore Sikh
beliefs about death,

12
00:00:28.490 --> 00:00:31.230
and rites in Punjab and Britain today.

13
00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:35.780
Your mission: find out why Sikhs marry
by walking round their scripture,

14
00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:38.270
and why there are no Sikh gravestones.
